theorem wd_odd {q : ℕ} (e : ℕ) (j : Fin (e + 1) → ZMod q) (i : Fin (2 * e + 1 + 1))
    (h : (i : ℕ) % 2 = 1) : wd e j i = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1 := by
  unfold wd
  rw [if_neg (by omega)]

/- English proof (translation)
Separate the alternatives or extract the components of the hypothesis. Establish an intermediate fact. Use linear arithmetic over natural numbers and integers. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities.
-/
theorem wd_congr {q : ℕ} (e : ℕ) (j j' : Fin (e + 1) → ZMod q) (i : Fin (2 * e + 1 + 1))
    (h : ∀ k : Fin (e + 1), (i : ℕ) = 2 * k → j k = j' k) : wd e j i = wd e j' i := by
  rcases Nat.mod_two_eq_zero_or_one i with hi | hi
  · have hk : (i : ℕ) = 2 * ((⟨i / 2, by omega⟩ : Fin (e + 1)) : ℕ) := by
      show (i : ℕ) = 2 * (i / 2)
      omega
    rw [wd_even e j i _ hk, wd_even e j' i _ hk, h _ hk]
  · rw [wd_odd e j i hi, wd_odd e j' i hi]

/- English proof (translation)
Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Reduce the conclusion to the remaining proof obligations. Establish an intermediate fact. Fix the arbitrary inputs or assume the hypotheses. Apply function extensionality and compare values at an arbitrary argument.

Reduce the conclusion to the remaining proof obligations. Proceed by induction. Treat this case separately. Treat this case separately. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules.

Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules.
